AI notice: This has come from a session with Claude, i've done my best to keep it clean/concise, just thought you should know...

## Description

`propertyNames: { type: "string" }` inside an `anyOf`/`oneOf` branch makes the first serialization log Ajv strict-mode warnings. Output is correct. Zod 4 emits this shape for `z.record(z.string(), z.string()).nullable()` (see also samchungy/fastify-zod-openapi#347).

## Why it hurts

Ajv writes these with `console.warn`, so they bypass the app logger (e.g. Pino) and go to stderr as unstructured text. Log collectors classify stderr as `error`, so they appear as false errors and count towards error queries and monitors. The app cannot silence them: Fastify serializer compilers do not expose the `ajv` options.

## Reproduction (7.0.1; also seen on 6.1.1)

```js
const build = require("fast-json-stringify")

const stringify = build({
  type: "object",
  properties: {
    fields: {
      anyOf: [
        { type: "object", propertyNames: { type: "string" }, additionalProperties: { type: "string" } },
        { type: "null" },
      ],
    },
  },
})

// Ajv compiles anyOf branches lazily: warnings appear on the first call, not on build()
stringify({ fields: { a: "b" } })
```

```
strict mode: type "object" not allowed by context "string" at "__fjs_root_0#/properties/fields/anyOf/0/propertyNames" (strictTypes)
strict mode: missing type "object" for keyword "fjs_type" at "__fjs_root_0#/properties/fields/anyOf/0/propertyNames" (strictTypes)
strict mode: type "object" not allowed by context "string" at "__fjs_root_0#/propertyNames" (strictTypes)
strict mode: missing type "object" for keyword "fjs_type" at "__fjs_root_0#/propertyNames" (strictTypes)
```

No warnings without `propertyNames`, or without the `anyOf` wrapper.

## Cause

`convertSchemaToAjvFormat` (`lib/validator.js`) rewrites every `type: "string"` to `["string", "object"]` plus `fjs_type`, so `toJSON()` values such as `Date` validate. It also recurses into `propertyNames`, where keys are always strings, so Ajv `strictTypes` rejects the added `object` type.

## Suggested fix

```diff
     for (const property in schema) {
-      if (typeof schema[property] === "object") {
+      if (property !== "propertyNames" && typeof schema[property] === "object") {
         this.convertSchemaToAjvFormat(schema[property])
       }
     }
```

Checked by overriding the method in memory on 7.0.1: warnings gone, output unchanged, `Date` in `anyOf: [{ type: "string" }, { type: "null" }]` still serializes. Existing test suite not run. Happy to open a PR with a regression test.

