RESULT: send() still blocked after 60s. fcm-caller stack:
    at org.apache.hc.core5.concurrent.BasicFuture.get(BasicFuture.java:97)
    at com.google.firebase.internal.ApacheHttp2Request.execute(ApacheHttp2Request.java:134)
    at com.google.api.client.http.HttpRequest.execute(HttpRequest.java:1012)
    at com.google.firebase.internal.ErrorHandlingHttpClient.send(ErrorHandlingHttpClient.java:97)
    ...
    at com.google.firebase.messaging.FirebaseMessaging.send(FirebaseMessaging.java:91)
```

On 9.5.0 with httpcore5 5.3.6, the dispatcher dies with `java.lang.NoSuchMethodError: 'void org.apache.hc.core5.http2.impl.nio.ClientH2UpgradeHandler.<init>(org.apache.hc.core5.http2.impl.nio.ClientH2StreamMultiplexerFactory)'` at `HttpAsyncClientProtocolNegotiationStarter.createHandler`. `send()` blocks at `ApacheHttp2Request.java:123`.

#### Relevant Code:

```java
