body_text:
### Feature Description

The go-redis package is capable of using client certificates, enabling mutual TLS. I have made a small change that allows specifying client certificate & private key in the Redis connection string in app.ini. Would you be interested in a pull request?

This is the code, in `manager_redis.go`:

```golang
clientCert := uri.Query().Get("tlscert")
clientKey := uri.Query().Get("tlskey")

if len(clientCert) > 0 && len(clientKey) > 0 {
  // Load the keypair.
  cert, err := tls.LoadX509KeyPair(clientCert, clientKey)
  if err != nil {
    log.Fatal("Error loading client certificate and/or key.")
  }
  tlsConfig.Certificates = []tls.Certificate{cert}
}

caCertPath := uri.Query().Get("cacert")

if len(caCertPath) > 0 {
  caCert, err := os.ReadFile(caCertPath)
  if err != nil {
    log.Fatal("Error loading CA certificate.")
  }
  caCertPool := x509.NewCertPool()
  caCertPool.AppendCertsFromPEM(caCert)
  tlsConfig.RootCAs = caCertPool
}
```

