```shell
N/A
```

### What did you do?

```go
package main

import (
	"io"
	"io/fs"
	iofs "io/fs"
	"testing"
	"testing/fstest"
)

type zobFS struct{}

func (zobFS) Open(path string) (iofs.File, error) {
	if path == "." {
		return new(rootDir), nil
	}
	return nil, &iofs.PathError{Op: "open", Path: path, Err: fs.ErrNotExist}
}

type rootDir bool

func (d *rootDir) Close() error {
	*d = true
	return nil
}

func (rootDir) Stat() (iofs.FileInfo, error) {
	panic("Stat not implemented!")
}

func (d *rootDir) ReadDir(n int) ([]iofs.DirEntry, error) {
	if *d { // closed
		return nil, iofs.ErrClosed
	}
	if n <= 0 {
		return nil, nil
	}
	return nil, io.EOF
}

func (rootDir) Read(b []byte) (int, error) {
	panic("Read not implemented")
}

func TestZobFS(t *testing.T) {
	if err := fstest.TestFS(zobFS{}); err != nil { // Should panic with "Stat not implemented"
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
}
```

### What did you see happen?

Run on the Go Playground: https://go.dev/play/p/tcKL92KEAFB

```console
$ go test
=== RUN   TestZobFS
--- PASS: TestZobFS (0.00s)
PASS
```

[testing/fstest.TestFS](https://pkg.go.dev/testing/fstest#TestFS) didn't call the `Stat` method, so the panic didn't occur. So it hansn't done any check the FileInfo returned.


### What did you expect to see?

The panic in rootDir.Stat should have been triggered.


TestFS should:
* [`Open(".")`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#FS.Open) and call [`Stat()`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#File.Stat) on the resulting file
* Check that the [`FileInfo`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#FileInfo) returned has [ModeDir](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#ModeDir) set for [`Mode()`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#FileInfo.Mode) and that [`IsDir()`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#FileInfo.IsDir) returns `true`.
* if fsys also implements [`ReadLinkFS`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#ReadLinkFS), check that [`Lstat`](https://pkg.go.dev/io/fs#ReadLinkFS.Lstat) returns a `FileInfo` with the same properties.

I'll provide a fix.

