body_text:
### Proposal Details

Linux has introduced yet another operation that can require tweaking in between fork and exec: core scheduling. Full docs are at https://docs.kernel.org/admin-guide/hw-vuln/core-scheduling.html. Relevant for Go is the equivalent to "coresched new COMMAND" or "coresched copy -s PID COMMAND" (see https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man1/coresched.1.html).

I propose adding the following to `syscall.SysProcAttr`:

```Go
