body_text:
### Proposal Details

I find myself doing this again and again:

```go
// `wrapped` is a sql.Null[string]
var unwrapped string
if wrapped.Valid {
  unwrapped = wrapped.V
}
// ...use unwrapped...
```

To make this more concise, it would be nice to have a guarantee that when `wrapped.Valid` is false after a call to `Scan`, `wrapped.V` is the zero value. This goes for `sql.Null` as well as for `sql.NullBool`, `sql.NullString`, etc.

An alternative is to add a safe `Unwrap` method to those types, returning the wrapped value when valid and the zero value when not.

